SUMMARY:Lunchbox Lecture Raleigh: NC's Capital of Baseball
DESCRIPTION:Take a journey through the rich history of baseball in Raleigh and the Triangle as we explore the game’s past\, present\, and exciting future in North Carolina’s capital.\nFrom legendary players and memorable moments to the region’s thriving minor league traditions\, discover how baseball has shaped our communities—and why Raleigh continues to be a compelling contender for Major League Baseball. \nDavid Gill is the Site Manager of Moore Square in downtown Raleigh. A Raleigh native\, he holds a B.A. in History and Political Science from Appalachian State University and has spent much of his career in the museum and public history fields. A lifelong baseball fan\, David enjoys exploring the stories\, people\, and history that have made the game an enduring part of North Carolina’s culture.
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/lunchbox-lecture-raleigh-ncs-capital-of-baseball/
LOCATION:City of Raleigh Museum\, 220 Fayetteville Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Humanities Sector Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/NEWLunchboxLectureFlyer_September_DavidGill_Print.png
ORGANIZER;CN="The City of Raleigh Museum":MAILTO:cormuseum@gmail.com
GEO:35.7776508;-78.6397629
