SUMMARY:North Carolina Literary Hall of Fame Induction Ceremony
DESCRIPTION:This fall the North Carolina Literary Hall of Fame will welcome not only writers but literary citizens\, of North Carolina and the world. \nD. G. Martin\, Michael Parker\, Shannon Ravenel\, David Sedaris\, and Daniel Wallace will join the Hall in a ceremony on October 4 at the Weymouth Center in Southern Pines. \nThe North Carolina Literary Hall of Fame celebrates and promotes the state’s rich literary heritage by commemorating its leading authors and encouraging the continued flourishing of great literature. Inductions are held every other year. A list of the 75 current inductees\, as well as samples of their work and video clips of past inductions\, can be found online at www.nclhof.org. \nThis event is free and open to the public.
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/north-carolina-literary-hall-of-fame-induction-ceremony/
LOCATION:Weymouth Center for the Arts & Humanities\, 555 E. Connecticut Avenue\, Sothern Pines\, NC\, 28387
CATEGORIES:NC Humanities Partner Program Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/avif:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/26listnopic.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="North Carolina Writers' Network":MAILTO:ed@ncwriters.org
GEO:35.1703089;-79.382786
